Hey, Jack.

276
00:18:58,596 --> 00:19:00,015
Faker.

277
00:19:01,182 --> 00:19:03,810
Jack, you're in charge now.

278
00:19:03,893 --> 00:19:07,814
This is my very special watch
so you can keep track of the time.

279
00:19:07,897 --> 00:19:10,692
Don't go out, Mom, please.

280
00:19:15,613 --> 00:19:16,990
Good night.

281
00:19:25,081 --> 00:19:29,210
Dear night lights,
protect my sleeping babes.

282
00:19:29,210 --> 00:19:32,589
Burn clear and steadfast tonight.

283
00:19:36,509 --> 00:19:39,304
l read recently that they're
now using lawyers instead of rats...

284
00:19:39,387 --> 00:19:41,306
for scientific experiments.

285
00:19:42,515 --> 00:19:44,100
They do this for two reasons.

286
00:19:44,184 --> 00:19:47,896
One, the scientists become
less attached to the lawyers.

287
00:19:49,397 --> 00:19:52,692
And two, there are certain things
that even rats won't do.

288
00:19:59,199 --> 00:20:02,702
l want to thank the board of trustees
of the Great Ormond Street Hospital...

289
00:20:02,786 --> 00:20:06,289
for having me here this evening,
and beg your forgiveness...

290
00:20:06,414 --> 00:20:09,292
because normally l'm used to
addressing shareholders.

291
00:20:11,920 --> 00:20:13,004
We don't know each other, and l doubt
that we have very much in common...

292
00:20:13,004 --> 00:20:17,092
We don't know each other, and l doubt
that we have very much in common...

293
00:20:17,092 --> 00:20:20,512
except this wonderful woman,
Wendy Angela Darling.

294
00:20:23,807 --> 00:20:26,017
Granny Wendy brought me
in from the cold.

295
00:20:26,101 --> 00:20:28,395
She taught me to read and write.

296
00:20:28,520 --> 00:20:31,606
She even found people
to be my parents and adopt me.

297
00:20:33,817 --> 00:20:35,485
She's loved so many children...

298
00:20:35,610 --> 00:20:36,111
just so efforlet-- effors--
effortlessly.

299
00:20:36,111 --> 00:20:40,198
just so efforlet-- effors--
effortlessly.

300
00:20:40,198 --> 00:20:42,701
That's her achievement.

301
00:20:42,784 --> 00:20:45,620
Many of you here tonight
were once lost children...

302
00:20:45,703 --> 00:20:49,499
but Granny Wendy found parents
and homes for each of you...

303
00:20:49,582 --> 00:20:52,210
and saved you--
that's her miracle.

304
00:20:53,420 --> 00:20:56,715
And l know that if you could stand now
you would express...

305
00:20:56,798 --> 00:21:00,302
much better than l have
your feelings of...

306
00:21:00,385 --> 00:21:01,803
gratitude...

307
00:21:04,597 --> 00:21:06,015
appreciation...

308
00:21:08,601 --> 00:21:11,312
and warm feelings...

309
00:21:11,396 --> 00:21:13,314
for this wonderful woman.

310
00:21:28,913 --> 00:21:31,082
l guess we do have
something in common.

311
00:21:33,793 --> 00:21:35,211
We're orphans.

312
00:21:55,315 --> 00:21:56,816
Hook!

313
00:23:17,689 --> 00:23:19,399
Are you all right?

314
00:23:36,916 --> 00:23:39,085
Thank you, Nigel-- Norman?

315
00:23:39,085 --> 00:23:42,213
- Neville, sir.
- Neville. ls that English?

316
00:23:42,297 --> 00:23:43,882
Merry Christmas.

317
00:23:46,009 --> 00:23:48,219
- l was proud of you.
- Really?

318
00:23:48,219 --> 00:23:50,180
lt was a beautiful speech.

319
00:24:07,280 --> 00:24:08,698
Hello?

320
00:24:19,918 --> 00:24:22,504
My God. The children.

321
00:24:27,717 --> 00:24:30,303
Maggie? Jack, answer me!

322
00:24:34,307 --> 00:24:37,894
The wind came up,
the door closed on me...

323
00:24:38,019 --> 00:24:40,605
