that was when you decided
not to go back to Neverland.

380
00:28:41,805 --> 00:28:42,806
Where?

381
00:28:43,890 --> 00:28:46,101
To Never-Neverland.

382
00:28:47,310 --> 00:28:48,812
Moira! l'm getting Moira.

383
00:28:48,895 --> 00:28:52,190
- l've tried to tell you so many times--
- Maybe the tea's ready.

384
00:28:52,315 --> 00:28:55,819
- l knew you'd forgotten.
- l'm not ready to deal with this now.

385
00:28:55,902 --> 00:29:00,115
The stories are true,
l swear to you.

386
00:29:00,115 --> 00:29:02,993
l swear on everything l adore.

387
00:29:03,118 --> 00:29:06,287
And now he's come back
to seek his revenge.

388
00:29:06,413 --> 00:29:08,999
The fight isn't over
for Captain James Hook.

389
00:29:08,999 --> 00:29:12,085
He wants you back. He knows
you'll follow Maggie and Jack...

390
00:29:12,085 --> 00:29:12,919
to the ends of the earth and beyond,
and by heaven you must find a way.

391
00:29:12,919 --> 00:29:18,508
to the ends of the earth and beyond,
and by heaven you must find a way.

392
00:29:18,508 --> 00:29:21,511
Only you can save your children.

393
00:29:23,304 --> 00:29:26,099
Somehow you must go back.

394
00:29:27,183 --> 00:29:30,020
You must make yourself remember.

395
00:29:32,313 --> 00:29:34,107
Remember what?

396
00:29:36,401 --> 00:29:39,487
Peter, don't you know who you are?

397
00:30:01,217 --> 00:30:02,594
Yes, boy.

398
00:30:20,695 --> 00:30:22,113
Sorry.

399
00:30:31,206 --> 00:30:32,582
Parachute.

400
00:31:19,879 --> 00:31:22,716
Firefly from hell!

401
00:31:24,509 --> 00:31:26,219
Big damn bug!

402
00:31:38,982 --> 00:31:41,693
Oh, it is you, it is!
A big you.

403
00:31:41,818 --> 00:31:44,404
l guess it's not bad that you're big.
You were always bigger than me.

404
00:31:44,487 --> 00:31:46,781
But now maybe this means
you'll be twice as much fun.

405
00:31:48,616 --> 00:31:50,410
What fun we'll have again!
What times!

406
00:31:50,493 --> 00:31:51,911
What great games!

407
00:31:56,082 --> 00:31:57,917
You're a little f--

408
00:31:59,586 --> 00:32:01,087
Fairy.

409
00:32:05,216 --> 00:32:06,301
Pixie.

410
00:32:06,301 --> 00:32:09,095
And if less is more,
there's no end to me, Peter Pan.

411
00:32:09,179 --> 00:32:11,598
- Peter Banning.
- Pan.

412
00:32:11,598 --> 00:32:13,808
Whoever you are,
it's still you.

413
00:32:13,892 --> 00:32:16,603
'Cause only one person
has that smell.

414
00:32:16,686 --> 00:32:17,979
Smell?

415
00:32:18,104 --> 00:32:20,690
The smell of someone who's ridden
the back of the wind, Peter.

416
00:32:20,815 --> 00:32:23,318
The smell of a hundred fun summers
of sleeping in trees...

417
00:32:23,401 --> 00:32:25,487
adventures with lndians and pirates.

418
00:32:25,612 --> 00:32:29,282
Oh, remember, Peter? The world was ours.
We could do everything or nothing.

419
00:32:29,282 --> 00:32:32,285
All l had to be was anything,
'cause it was always us.

420
00:32:34,120 --> 00:32:34,496
Oh, no. lt's finally happened.
