- Rufio, hit him back.

976
01:15:03,086 --> 01:15:04,003
Mung tongue.

977
01:15:05,380 --> 01:15:07,298
- Math tutor.
- Pinhead.

978
01:15:08,299 --> 01:15:09,801
- Prison barber.
- Mother lover.

979
01:15:09,884 --> 01:15:12,512
- Nearsighted gynecologist.
- ln your face, camel cake!

980
01:15:12,595 --> 01:15:16,099
- ln your rear, cow derriere.
- Lying, crying, spying ultra-pig!

981
01:15:16,182 --> 01:15:18,310
You lewd, crude, rude
bag-of-prechewed-food dude.

982
01:15:18,393 --> 01:15:20,187
Bangerang, Peter!

983
01:15:22,397 --> 01:15:25,692
You-- You man!
Stupid, stupid man!

984
01:15:25,817 --> 01:15:28,820
lf l'm a maggot burger,
why don't you just eat me?

985
01:15:28,903 --> 01:15:31,489
You two-toned, zebra-headed,
slime-coated...

986
01:15:31,614 --> 01:15:34,993
pimple-farmin', paramecium brain,
munchin' on your own mucus...

987
01:15:35,118 --> 01:15:37,204
suffering from Peter Pan envy!

988
01:15:37,287 --> 01:15:38,914
What's a paramecium brain?

989
01:15:38,997 --> 01:15:42,083
l'll tell you what a paramecium is.
That's a paramecium!

990
01:15:42,208 --> 01:15:45,587
lt's a one-celled critter
with no brain that can't fly!

991
01:15:45,712 --> 01:15:48,715
Don't mess with me, man.
l'm a lawyer!

992
01:15:48,798 --> 01:15:50,592
Banning. Banning.

993
01:15:55,388 --> 01:15:58,099
Rufio! Rufio!

994
01:15:58,099 --> 01:16:00,519
Banning is bangerang!

995
01:16:04,105 --> 01:16:04,397
Oh, Rufio, why don't you just
go suck on a dead dog's nose?

996
01:16:04,397 --> 01:16:16,618
Oh, Rufio, why don't you just
go suck on a dead dog's nose?

997
01:16:16,618 --> 01:16:19,412
- You're doing it.
- Doing what?

998
01:16:19,496 --> 01:16:22,082
Using your imagination, Peter.

999
01:16:48,107 --> 01:16:51,111
You're playing with us, Peter.

1000
01:16:51,194 --> 01:16:53,196
You're doing it.

1001
01:17:14,884 --> 01:17:16,803
Drink your poe-poe, Peter.

1002
01:17:18,597 --> 01:17:21,099
How is it?

1003
01:17:21,182 --> 01:17:22,601
Bangerang.

1004
01:17:24,603 --> 01:17:25,979
Catch !

1005
01:17:33,820 --> 01:17:36,489
Hey, Pockets, catch!

1006
01:17:37,615 --> 01:17:39,993
Oh, Don't Ask.

1007
01:17:53,882 --> 01:17:55,508
Bangerang!

1008
01:18:03,517 --> 01:18:05,894
Hey, Pan the Man, catch this!

1009
01:18:05,894 --> 01:18:08,313
- Peter, look out!
- Watch out!

1010
01:18:40,887 --> 01:18:42,597
Bangerang.

1011
01:18:58,613 --> 01:19:02,701
Peter, can l talk to you?

1012
01:19:02,701 --> 01:19:04,619
Sure, Thud.

1013
01:19:05,704 --> 01:19:07,581
l remember Tootles.

1014
01:19:07,706 --> 01:19:09,708
- You do?
- He was lost too.

1015
01:19:09,791 --> 01:19:12,085
How could you know Tootles?

1016
01:19:12,210 --> 01:19:14,587
He was a Lost Boy.

1017
01:19:14,587 --> 01:19:16,798
These are his marbles.

1018
01:19:18,383 --> 01:19:21,011
These are his happy thoughts.

1019
01:19:28,810 --> 01:19:32,605
- He really did lose his marbles.
- Yeah, he lost 'em good.

1020
01:19:35,316 --> 01:19:37,402
- Peter, you know what?
- What?

1021
01:19:37,485 --> 01:19:40,697
My happy thought will help you.

1022
01:19:40,780 --> 01:19:42,907
What's your happy thought, Thud?

1023
01:19:43,783 --> 01:19:46,703
Mine's my mother.

1024
01:19:46,786 --> 01:19:49,581
Do you remember
your mother, Peter?

1025
01:19:49,706 --> 01:19:51,583
Wish l could.

1026
01:19:54,210 --> 01:19:55,587
Listen.

1027
01:20:04,012 --> 01:20:04,387
At night when l'm alone

1028
01:20:04,387 --> 01:20:08,391
At night when l'm alone

1029
01:20:08,391 --> 01:20:11,686
l lie awake and wonder

1030
01:20:11,812 --> 01:20:13,479
My mom sang that song.

1031
01:20:13,605 --> 01:20:14,188
My young Jack, tell me about the game
of baseball. l can't remember.

1032
01:20:14,188 --> 01:20:18,318
My young Jack, tell me about the game
of baseball. l can't remember.

1033
01:20:18,318 --> 01:20:21,780
Are the mates standin'
or are they on horseback?

1034
01:20:23,907 --> 01:20:24,908
The stars are all my friends

1035
01:20:24,908 --> 01:20:28,995
The stars are all my friends

1036
01:20:28,995 --> 01:20:32,916
Till the nighttime ends

1037
01:20:32,999 --> 01:20:33,500
So l know l'm not alone

1038
01:20:33,500 --> 01:20:37,587
So l know l'm not alone

1039
01:20:37,587 --> 01:20:40,006
When l'm here

1040
01:20:40,006 --> 01:20:42,384
On my own

1041
01:20:42,509 --> 01:20:42,884
lsn't that a wonder

1042
01:20:42,884 --> 01:20:47,013
lsn't that a wonder

1043
01:20:47,013 --> 01:20:47,305
When you're alone

1044
01:20:47,305 --> 01:20:51,309
When you're alone

1045
01:20:51,309 --> 01:20:55,188
You're not alone

1046
01:20:55,313 --> 01:20:56,689
Not really alone

1047
01:20:56,689 --> 01:21:44,696
Not really alone

1048
01:21:44,696 --> 01:21:47,407
Good night, Neverland!

1049
01:22:25,904 --> 01:22:28,615
What is it?
l hear it again.

1050
01:22:30,116 --> 01:22:32,911
Smee, is that crocodile
back from the dead?

1051
01:22:33,995 --> 01:22:35,997
Tick-tock, tick-tock.

1052
01:22:38,416 --> 01:22:40,418
ls that the clock?

1053
01:22:42,712 --> 01:22:46,299
You killed that croc years ago, Captain.
We smash every clock we find.

1054
01:22:46,382 --> 01:22:48,802
The little elf
didn't know any better.

1055
01:22:51,304 --> 01:22:53,014
To the museum at once.

1056
01:23:06,986 --> 01:23:07,695
Shine 'em up! Put a fresh coat
of varnish on your peg right here!

1057
01:23:07,695 --> 01:23:11,700
Shine 'em up! Put a fresh coat
of varnish on your peg right here!

1058
01:23:11,700 --> 01:23:15,412
Treasure maps!
Authentic treasure maps!

1059
01:23:25,088 --> 01:23:27,215
Broken clocks.

1060
01:23:27,298 --> 01:23:27,715
Each one ticked its last tock,
and now all is well.

1061
01:23:27,715 --> 01:23:32,887
Each one ticked its last tock,
and now all is well.

1062
01:23:32,887 --> 01:23:35,599
- Just listen.
- l don't hear anything.

1063
01:23:36,892 --> 01:23:40,020
l know!
Good form. Exactly.

1064
01:23:40,103 --> 01:23:42,897
Jack, you see this?
Come over here.

1065
01:23:42,981 --> 01:23:46,693
You can take it. This is Barbecue's
very own bedside clock.

1066
01:23:46,693 --> 01:23:48,987
He was quite an infamous pirate.

1067
01:23:48,987 --> 01:23:52,907
l smashed this clock
immediately after l gutted him.

1068
01:23:52,991 --> 01:23:56,620
And his ship made
such a pretty bonfire on the waves.

1069
01:24:04,210 --> 01:24:05,795
What is that...

1070
01:24:05,879 --> 01:24:07,505
l hear?

1071
01:24:09,090 --> 01:24:11,009
A ticking!

1072
01:24:12,510 --> 01:24:15,096
Smee, stop it!
Stop the ticking!

1073
01:24:15,180 --> 01:24:17,515
Stop it! Stop that tick!

1074
01:24:19,309 --> 01:24:22,020
There's no tickin' here.
There's nothin' left to tick.

1075
01:24:24,105 --> 01:24:26,191
Oh, my God.

1076
01:24:26,316 --> 01:24:27,192
This is for the ticking
that might have been.

1077
01:24:27,192 --> 01:24:31,279
This is for the ticking
that might have been.

1078
01:24:31,279 --> 01:24:34,199
- Abso-floggin'-lutely!
- Get his father's watch.

1079
01:24:36,993 --> 01:24:38,787
Go on.

1080
01:24:38,912 --> 01:24:42,499
You know you want to.
Give it a try.

1081
01:24:43,500 --> 01:24:45,001
Go on.

1082
01:24:45,001 --> 01:24:47,295
This is for...

1083
01:24:47,295 --> 01:24:50,090
never letting me blow bubbles
in my chocolate milk!

1084
01:24:51,091 --> 01:24:53,593
- Yes!
- Good form! Bravo!

1085
01:24:53,593 --> 01:24:55,720
Here you go.
lsn't that wonderful?

1086
01:24:55,804 --> 01:24:59,307
This is for never letting me
jump on my own bed.

1087
01:25:00,308 --> 01:25:03,186
Make time stand still, laddie.

1088
01:25:03,311 --> 01:25:07,106
For always making promises
and breaking them.

1089
01:25:07,190 --> 01:25:09,484
For never doing anything with me.

1090
01:25:11,111 --> 01:25:13,488
For a father who's
never there, Jack.

1091
01:25:16,700 --> 01:25:20,495
Jack, for a father
who didn't save you on the ship.

1092
01:25:21,496 --> 01:25:23,582
He wouldn't save us.

1093
01:25:23,707 --> 01:25:26,000
Who couldn't save you, Jack.

1094
01:25:26,000 --> 01:25:29,712
He-- He wouldn't.
He didn't even try.

1095
01:25:29,796 --> 01:25:33,091
He was there and we were there,
and he wouldn't try.

1096
01:25:36,219 --> 01:25:39,180
Jack, he will try.

1097
01:25:41,182 --> 01:25:43,602
And the question will be...

1098
01:25:43,685 --> 01:25:47,188
when the time comes,
do you want to be saved?

1099
01:25:48,606 --> 01:25:50,692
Don't you answer now.

1100
01:25:50,817 --> 01:25:54,487
Now it's time to be
whatever you want to be.

1101
01:25:56,197 --> 01:25:58,783
Put behind you
any thoughts of home...

1102
01:25:58,908 --> 01:26:01,703
that place of broken promises.

1103
01:26:02,704 --> 01:26:03,788
That what?

1104
01:26:05,207 --> 01:26:08,418
Have l ever made a promise, Jack...

1105
01:26:08,501 --> 01:26:11,504
l have not kept?

1106
01:26:14,090 --> 01:26:16,092
Have l, son?

1107
01:26:44,412 --> 01:26:46,790
Come on. Let's go.

1108
01:26:55,006 --> 01:26:56,716
l don't like this game.

1109
01:26:56,800 --> 01:26:59,886
Steal Hook's hook
as fast as you can.

1110
01:27:00,011 --> 01:27:01,888
lt'll make you proud.

1111
01:27:02,013 --> 01:27:05,183
Then you'll crow like Pan.

1112
01:27:05,308 --> 01:27:16,486
Confound it, Druscilla, glove me.
The game is about to start.

1113
01:27:16,486 --> 01:27:19,489
l need my bubbly.
Give me my bubbly.

1114
01:27:24,786 --> 01:27:27,205
Steal Hook's hook, then crow.

1115
01:27:47,184 --> 01:27:48,894
Jackie, boy!

1116
01:27:49,019 --> 01:27:52,105
This is for all the games
your daddy missed.

1117
01:27:53,189 --> 01:27:56,109
Hook would never
miss your games, son.

1118
01:27:56,192 --> 01:27:58,111
You're almost there.
Just take it.

1119
01:27:58,194 --> 01:28:00,780
- What's he looking at?
- You're this close.

1120
01:28:00,905 --> 01:28:03,116
What's the matter?
lt's right there.

1121
01:28:03,199 --> 01:28:04,618
Grab it.

1122
01:28:06,912 --> 01:28:09,080
Come on, Jack.

1123
01:28:09,206 --> 01:28:11,082
And-a-one...

1124
01:28:12,792 --> 01:28:15,503
and-a-two,
and a toodle-loodle-loo!

1125
01:28:21,718 --> 01:28:23,011
Strike!

1126
01:28:23,094 --> 01:28:33,688
Wait for the good pitches.

1127
01:28:33,688 --> 01:28:39,319
Jack, Jack, he's our man!
lf he can't do it, nobody can !

1128
01:28:39,319 --> 01:28:40,779
He's stealing second!

1129
01:28:45,492 --> 01:28:47,494
Stop it!

1130
01:28:47,494 --> 01:28:51,581
We're playing this game according
to Master Jack's rules. Bad form.

1131
01:28:51,581 --> 01:28:54,208
Sit down now.
Let's resume the game.

1132
01:28:54,208 --> 01:28:56,419
Very violent sport,
isn't it, baseball?

1133
01:29:03,510 --> 01:29:06,304
Run home, Jack!
Run home, Jack!

1134
01:29:13,603 --> 01:29:15,480
''Run home, Jack.''

1135
01:29:15,605 --> 01:29:19,692
Smee! No!
They've got it backwards!

1136
01:29:19,692 --> 01:29:21,694
Tell them to turn it around!

1137
01:29:21,694 --> 01:29:23,613
Maggie?

1138
01:29:23,697 --> 01:29:25,782
Switch !

1139
01:29:30,120 --> 01:29:32,706
Home run, Jack!

1140
01:29:34,708 --> 01:29:37,085
Home run, Jack.

1141
01:29:45,301 --> 01:29:47,387
He can't hit the curve.

1142
01:30:12,579 --> 01:30:14,915
My Jack!

1143
01:30:16,916 --> 01:30:18,209
My Jack.

1144
01:30:27,510 --> 01:30:30,305
You did it!
Hoist him up!

1145
01:30:34,684 --> 01:30:37,895
That's my boy!
You did it, son!

1146
01:30:47,280 --> 01:30:49,908
Two, four, six, eight!

1147
01:30:49,991 --> 01:30:52,285
Who do we appreciate?

1148
01:30:52,410 --> 01:30:54,579
Jack! Jack!

1149
01:31:16,017 --> 01:31:18,103
Gotta fly.

1150
01:31:20,396 --> 01:31:22,398
Happy thought.

1151
01:31:23,983 --> 01:31:26,694
One great big happy thought.

1152
01:31:26,820 --> 01:31:28,780
Less is more.

1153
01:31:30,615 --> 01:31:31,992
l can!

1154
01:33:03,416 --> 01:33:06,085
''Tootles, Wendy...

1155
01:33:06,085 --> 01:33:32,695
John, Michael, Peter.''

1156
01:33:32,695 --> 01:33:36,616
Be careful, Peter.
You're a lot taller than you used to be.

1157
01:33:37,909 --> 01:33:39,995
Well, say something.

1158
01:33:42,080 --> 01:33:44,708
Do you like my dress?

1159
01:33:48,503 --> 01:33:50,380
You look beautiful.

1160
01:33:55,885 --> 01:33:59,514
- What's the occasion?
- You are.

1161
01:34:00,515 --> 01:34:03,101
lt's a ''welcome home'' party.

1162
01:34:08,314 --> 01:34:11,192
- What happened here?
- Hook.

1163
01:34:11,317 --> 01:34:13,319
Burnt it when
you didn't come back.

1164
01:34:34,090 --> 01:34:35,717
Kiss.

1165
01:34:41,014 --> 01:34:42,599
Wendy.

1166
01:34:45,685 --> 01:34:49,480
This is Wendy's house.
Noodles and Nibs built it for her.

1167
01:34:52,692 --> 01:34:54,319
l remember.

1168
01:34:56,613 --> 01:34:59,282
- Wendy used to sit in that chair.
- Yes.

1169
01:34:59,282 --> 01:35:01,785
But it wasn't there.
lt was here.

1170
01:35:03,119 --> 01:35:05,288
We used to sit here
while she'd darn socks...

1171
01:35:05,413 --> 01:35:06,790
and tell us stories.

1172
01:35:08,083 --> 01:35:10,418
She slept here.

1173
01:35:10,501 --> 01:35:12,420
Tink, your apartment
was right here.

1174
01:35:12,504 --> 01:35:13,880
Yes.

1175
01:35:14,005 --> 01:35:19,386
Little Michael
had his basket bed right here.

1176
01:35:19,386 --> 01:35:21,096
John.

1177
01:35:28,812 --> 01:35:31,981
Taddy. My Taddy.

1178
01:35:36,986 --> 01:35:39,906
Mother used to put him in the pram
to keep me company.

1179
01:35:45,787 --> 01:35:47,914
l remember my mother.

1180
01:35:48,999 --> 01:35:50,792
l remember her.

1181
01:35:53,086 --> 01:35:56,381
You can be sure of
very fine schools indeed.

1182
01:35:56,506 --> 01:35:57,006
First he will attend Whitehall,
then Oxford...

1183
01:35:57,006 --> 01:36:01,094
First he will attend Whitehall,
then Oxford...

1184
01:36:01,094 --> 01:36:03,513
and of course,
after graduation...

1185
01:36:03,597 --> 01:36:07,309
he will prepare for a judgeship
in the highest court...

1186
01:36:07,392 --> 01:36:10,312
making time for marriage
and family...

1187
01:36:10,395 --> 01:36:13,815
and all of that,
just like his father.

1188
01:36:13,898 --> 01:36:16,401
lsn't that what grown-ups
want for their children?

1189
01:36:16,484 --> 01:36:18,486
l was afraid because
l didn't want to grow up...

1190
01:36:18,611 --> 01:36:22,115
because everybody who grows up
has to die someday.

1191
01:36:22,115 --> 01:36:24,117
So l ran away.

1192
01:36:34,586 --> 01:36:37,213
Tink...

1193
01:36:37,213 --> 01:36:40,008
you came and you saved me.

1194
01:36:40,008 --> 01:36:43,720
You brought me to Neverland.
You taught me to fly.

1195
01:36:46,806 --> 01:36:49,100
But l was still a little boy...

1196
01:36:49,184 --> 01:36:51,394
and l missed my mother...

1197
01:36:51,520 --> 01:36:54,480
so l decided to fly home
to my very own window.

1198
01:36:55,982 --> 01:36:59,486
But it was shut.
They'd forgotten about me.

1199
01:37:03,907 --> 01:37:06,284
l found other windows to visit...

1200
01:37:06,409 --> 01:37:09,496
ones that weren't
shut closed on me.

1201
01:37:09,579 --> 01:37:13,083
That's how l met Wendy.
l chased my shadow in her nursery.

1202
01:37:13,208 --> 01:37:28,390
l expected my shadow and l
would join together like drops of water.

1203
01:37:28,390 --> 01:37:30,016
Boy.

1204
01:37:32,519 --> 01:37:34,395
Why are you crying?

1205
01:37:36,689 --> 01:37:38,316
What's your name?

1206
01:37:39,484 --> 01:37:43,196
Wendy Moira Angela Darling.
What's yours?

1207
01:37:43,279 --> 01:37:50,287
l came back many times for Wendy,
always in the spring.

1208
01:37:50,287 --> 01:37:53,290
And Wendy kept getting older...

1209
01:37:53,415 --> 01:37:54,791
and older...

1210
01:37:54,916 --> 01:37:59,003
and then l came back
the last time.

1211
01:37:59,003 --> 01:38:01,714
Peter, l can't come with you.

1212
01:38:01,798 --> 01:38:04,092
l've forgotten how to fly.

1213
01:38:05,301 --> 01:38:07,220
l'm old, Peter.

1214
01:38:08,305 --> 01:38:11,516
Ever so much more than 20.

1215
01:38:11,600 --> 01:38:14,186
- l grew up a long time ago.
- No! No!

1216
01:38:14,311 --> 01:38:16,896
- You promised.
- l have children of my own now.

1217
01:38:16,896 --> 01:38:19,482
They have children of their own.

1218
01:38:19,482 --> 01:38:20,316
That's my grandchild, Moira,
asleep in the bed.

1219
01:38:20,316 --> 01:38:24,404
That's my grandchild, Moira,
asleep in the bed.

1220
01:38:24,404 --> 01:38:26,698
When l saw her
lying there sleeping...

1221
01:38:26,781 --> 01:38:29,784
that moment,
something changed in me forever.

1222
01:38:29,909 --> 01:38:32,120
l shall give her a kiss.

1223
01:38:33,288 --> 01:38:35,415
No, Peter.
No buttons.

1224
01:38:35,415 --> 01:38:37,000
No thimbles.

1225
01:38:37,083 --> 01:38:46,509
l couldn't bear Moira's heartbreak
when she finds she can't keep you.

1226
01:38:46,509 --> 01:38:49,387
l mean a real kiss.

1227
01:39:13,411 --> 01:39:16,581
