l know her.

1479
02:08:23,620 --> 02:08:26,206
She looks like an angel.

1480
02:08:26,289 --> 02:08:28,708
Let's not wake her yet.

1481
02:09:15,588 --> 02:09:16,005
Oh, my dear child.
Have you been up all night?

1482
02:09:16,005 --> 02:09:22,304
Oh, my dear child.
Have you been up all night?

1483
02:09:22,304 --> 02:09:26,182
l see them in their beds
so often in my dreams...

1484
02:09:26,182 --> 02:09:28,518
when l wake up,
they're still there.

1485
02:09:31,813 --> 02:09:32,814
Mommy!

1486
02:10:11,686 --> 02:10:13,187
Tink.

1487
02:10:24,282 --> 02:10:25,200
Hello.

1488
02:10:28,411 --> 02:10:41,091
Havin' trouble with the missus?
You will have by the time you get home.

1489
02:10:41,091 --> 02:10:46,680
Say it, Peter.
Say it and mean it.

1490
02:10:46,680 --> 02:10:48,807
l believe in fairies.

1491
02:10:48,890 --> 02:10:52,185
You know that place
between asleep and awake?

1492
02:10:52,310 --> 02:10:54,312
That place where
you still remember dreaming?

1493
02:10:56,397 --> 02:10:59,818
That's where
l'll always love you...

1494
02:10:59,901 --> 02:11:01,611
Peter Pan.

1495
02:11:04,280 --> 02:11:06,199
That's where l'll be waiting.

1496
02:11:26,302 --> 02:11:27,804
Nana!

1497
02:11:27,804 --> 02:11:31,391
Oh, give us a kiss.
Come here, you drool machine.

1498
02:11:31,516 --> 02:11:33,602
Maggie, Moira, Jack!

1499
02:11:58,209 --> 02:12:01,588
Brad, hi!
You've been holding this long?

1500
02:12:02,589 --> 02:12:05,008
l'm incredible. Yeah.

1501
02:12:05,091 --> 02:12:07,093
Neverland.

1502
02:12:07,218 --> 02:12:09,095
Lost Boys.

1503
02:12:09,179 --> 02:12:11,890
Jim Hook, duel to the death.
l'll fill you in later.

1504
02:12:11,890 --> 02:12:12,515
l'd love to chat, but l gotta
climb a drainpipe right now.

1505
02:12:12,515 --> 02:12:16,603
l'd love to chat, but l gotta
climb a drainpipe right now.

1506
02:12:16,603 --> 02:12:18,813
Why? 'Cause l ran out
of fairy dust.

1507
02:12:18,897 --> 02:12:21,399
lf not, l would've flown up.
''Why?''

1508
02:12:27,906 --> 02:12:31,201
- Mom, l fought pirates!
- You would've loved it there!

1509
02:12:32,410 --> 02:12:34,913
Maggie, Moira, Jack!
Granny Wendy!

1510
02:12:35,997 --> 02:12:38,583
Let me in. Please.

1511
02:12:41,711 --> 02:12:44,005
Excuse me.
Do you have an appointment?

1512
02:12:46,591 --> 02:12:49,594
What did l tell you
about this window?

1513
02:12:49,719 --> 02:12:51,304
Always keep it open !

1514
02:12:53,098 --> 02:12:55,809
Never, ever, ever close it!

1515
02:13:15,620 --> 02:13:17,289
l have to take this.

1516
02:13:17,289 --> 02:13:17,914
Brad, have you ever wondered what it's
like to feel the exhilaration of flying?

1517
02:13:17,914 --> 02:13:22,001
Brad, have you ever wondered what it's
like to feel the exhilaration of flying?

1518
02:13:22,001 --> 02:13:24,379
Feel this.

1519
02:13:24,504 --> 02:13:26,381
Where have you been?

1520
02:13:26,506 --> 02:13:29,217
- Fly me, Daddy!
- Anytime, Maggie!

1521
02:13:29,300 --> 02:13:31,886
To infinity and back again.

1522
02:13:32,012 --> 02:13:34,180
Hello, Peter.

1523
02:13:34,306 --> 02:13:37,184
l missed the adventure again,
didn't l?

1524
02:13:39,311 --> 02:13:42,397
l think these belong to you.

1525
02:13:53,700 --> 02:13:56,286
Look!
See! Look!

1526
02:13:56,286 --> 02:13:59,998
l didn't lose my marbles after all!
Wendy, look!

1527
02:14:00,081 --> 02:14:02,709
l didn't lose my marbles
after all!

1528
02:14:04,711 --> 02:14:06,588
Hello, boy.

1529
02:14:07,589 --> 02:14:11,217
Hello, Wendy lady.
Give us a squdge.

1530
02:14:22,187 --> 02:14:24,188
Boy, why are you crying?

1531
02:14:24,188 --> 02:14:27,901
l don't know.
A tear for every happy thought.

1532
02:14:27,984 --> 02:14:31,613
- One for me?
- One for me?

1533
02:14:31,696 --> 02:14:34,115
And one for me!

1534
02:14:48,797 --> 02:14:50,715
Seize the day!

1535
02:14:54,219 --> 02:14:57,514
So, your adventures are over.

1536
02:14:57,597 --> 02:15:00,892
Oh, no. To live--

1537
02:15:01,017 --> 02:15:03,812
To live would be
an awfully big adventure.
